== (a) delta rule: p after n consistent exposures, eta 0.35 (bench R2)
   n=1: p = 1 - 0.65^n = 0.350
   n=2: p = 1 - 0.65^n = 0.577
   n=3: p = 1 - 0.65^n = 0.725
   n=5: p = 1 - 0.65^n = 0.884
   n=8: p = 1 - 0.65^n = 0.968
== accumulator I += G*e + u (bound 1), u = 0.15
   G=1.0, e=0.6: step 0.75/tick -> release after 2 ticks
   G=0.8, e=0.6: step 0.63/tick -> release after 2 ticks
   G=1.0, e=0.0: step 0.15/tick -> release after 7 ticks
   G=0.3, e=0.3: step 0.24/tick -> release after 5 ticks
== soft log time bins [2^k, 2^(k+2)): which bins each delay activates
   tau=  1: bins [0]
   tau=  3: bins [0, 1]
   tau=  5: bins [1, 2]
   tau=  6: bins [1, 2]
   tau=  8: bins [2, 3]
   tau= 10: bins [2, 3]
   tau= 12: bins [2, 3]
   tau= 16: bins [3, 4]
   tau= 30: bins [3, 4]
   tau= 33: bins [4, 5]
   tau= 45: bins [4, 5]
   tau= 60: bins [4, 5]
== (b) restoration s = m + w*pi; accept if s >= 0.75; w = w_max*(1 - pi_ear)
   w_max 0.15, pi_ear 1.0: w = 0.000
   w_max 0.15, pi_ear 0.33: w = 0.100
   w_max 0.15, pi_ear 0.0: w = 0.150
   w=0.10 m=0.68 pi=0.85: s=0.765 -> accepted
   w=0.10 m=0.66 pi=0.85: s=0.745 -> not accepted
   w=0.10 m=0.7 pi=0.6: s=0.760 -> accepted
   w=0.10 m=0.62 pi=0.1: s=0.630 -> not accepted
   w=0.10 m=0.7 pi=0.3: s=0.730 -> not accepted
   clean window vs another lexicon char: 0.96 - 0.77 = 0.19 > w_max 0.15 -> never overridden
== eligibility decay e^(-dt/tau_e), tau_e = 20 ticks
   dt=5: 0.78
   dt=11: 0.58
   dt=16: 0.45
   dt=25: 0.29
   dt=32: 0.20
   dt=45: 0.11
== learned NoGo after late-start overlaps: step = eta_v * |delta| * e, eta_v 0.2, |delta| 0.5, e 0.5
   step 0.050 per event -> 10 events to move Go-NoGo by 0.5
== pure-neuron build, s = 1 (ASSUMED sizes; synapses = units x fan-in)
   EAR0 (fixed local 3-D)             units   1920  synapses   0.01 M
   SYL assemblies (k=16)              units   2048  synapses   0.13 M
   VOICE                              units    256  synapses   0.02 M
   EYE (adapting)                     units   1024  synapses   0.00 M
   VR eye->word                       units   2048  synapses   0.07 M
   MEAN                               units    512  synapses   0.13 M
   LATEST (item x age x source)       units  16384  synapses   0.05 M
   THOUGHT (persistent)               units   4096  synapses   0.26 M
   TIME + P4 detectors                units     64  synapses   0.00 M
   MIX conjunctions                   units  48000  synapses   0.43 M
   GEN out (fan-out 64 from MIX)      units   2049  synapses   3.07 M
   M4 gates + critic (event-driven: 480 active inputs) units     11  synapses   0.53 M
   motor programs + forward/inverse   units   2048  synapses   0.26 M
   DG                                 units   6000  synapses   0.07 M
   CA3 (fixed fan-in 1000)            units  10000  synapses  10.00 M
   CA1 -> cortex                      units  10000  synapses   0.64 M
   total units 106 k, synapses 15.7 M, lit synaptic events per speech tick ~0.16 M
   memory (4 B weight + 4 B index per synapse) ~125 MB at s=1, ~502 MB at s=4
   CPU numpy, s=1: ~498 s per 1e6-tick life (speech 328 + silent 170)
   CPU numpy, s=4: ~1,993 s per 1e6-tick life (speech 1,313 + silent 680)
   born-wired calibration: 750k cells / 2M synapses at 13.3 ms per tick, unbatched consumer GPU -> 1e6 ticks = 13,300 s if a v3 agent cost the same per tick
== lineage loop on the A800 CPU runner (4 processes x 90 min per job)
   one life + probes 1630 s -> 12 lives per job; P=12 per generation -> 1 job/generation
   10 generations x 2 lineages = 20 jobs ~ 15 h wall at 2 slots
